# Campus Resource Intelligence

This file mirrors the main project overview for the project root and is aligned with the SRS v1.1 requirements.

## Overview
The system is a college resource-sharing platform that lets students discover and request underused equipment, labs, and spaces, while staff maintain approval authority, safety compliance, and accountability.

## Based on SRS
The system design and feature set are derived from the root document:
`SRS v1.1 Campus Resource Intelligence.md`

## Product goals
- Improve utilization of underused campus resources
- Provide a single place for resource discovery and request workflows
- Maintain staff control over approvals and moderation
- Enforce fairness with booking limits and waitlists
- Record handover, return, incidents, and conditions
- Provide auditable history and reporting

## Scope
- Single-college prototype
- Student, manager, department owner, and admin roles
- Equipment, spaces, and facilities management
- Booking lifecycle with approval, conflict prevention, and overbook protection
- QR/token-based handover and condition evidence
- Utilization analytics and audit trail

## Core stack
- React + Vite + Tailwind CSS
- Node.js + Express
- MongoDB
- Auth via server-side sessions or HTTP-only JWT cookies
- File storage for evidence and resource images
- Reminder scheduler for no-show and overdue workflows

## Note
This repository is still in planning and implementation setup based on the SRS. The core MVP focuses on the mandatory P0 and P1 requirements before optional enhancements.
